title: Reading corner: The Lighthouse at Coriel
from: Esme Walsh
gist: Reading corner read on in The Lighthouse at Coriel: chapters seven to twelve.
== lines
walsh-esme: Chapters seven to twelve. Who's caught up?
ibarra-rafael: Me. And chapter thirteen. By accident. Saying nothing.
soto-marta: Don't you dare.
strand-erik: She writes back in the log. And the log answers!
strand-erik: Different ink. Next morning. I had to put it down.
soto-marta: Footprints in the salt. A warm kettle. Somebody's there.
soto-marta: Ghosts don't boil kettles.
strand-erik: A lonely one might. To feel at home.   [laugh]
kowalczyk: Look at who polishes the lens. Every night.
walsh-esme: Ada sleeps through it. Chapter ten, page one forty.
ibarra-rafael: Chapter thirteen is very... no. Nothing. Biscuit?
walsh-esme > you: Should Ada keep writing back?
? choice
* Yes. Carefully.   rel:walsh-esme+1 flag:read.s2.1
  walsh-esme: Carefully. Like hot oil. Yes.
* No. Get on the boat and go.   rel:walsh-esme+1 flag:read.s2.2
  walsh-esme: Half this sofa is nodding. Don't encourage them.   [laugh]
* Ask it something only a keeper would know.   rel:walsh-esme+1 flag:read.s2.3
  walsh-esme: That's clever. Somebody here has gone very quiet.
walsh-esme: To chapter nineteen. Quietly. And stop at nineteen.
